=-\\mathbf{x} &  & [\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{axiom __}\\hspace{0.222em}\\hspace{0.222em}] \\\\ \\mathbf{y}+(\\mathbf{x}+(-\\mathbf{x})) & =-\\mathbf{x} &  & [\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{axiom __}\\hspace{0.222em}\\hspace{0.222em}] \\\\ \\mathbf{y}+\\mathbf{0} & =-\\mathbf{x} &  & [\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{axiom A4}\\hspace{0.222em}] \\\\ \\mathbf{y} & =-\\mathbf{x} &  & [\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{axiom A3}\\hspace{0.222em}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{ll}{\\color{black}\\text{[A1]}}:{\\color{blue}\\mathbf{x}+\\mathbf{y}=\\mathbf{y}+\\mathbf{x}} & {\\color{black}\\text{[A5]}}:{\\color{blue}1\\cdot \\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{x}} \\\\ {\\color{black}\\text{[A2]}}:{\\color{blue}(\\mathbf{x}+\\mathbf{y})+\\mathbf{z}=\\mathbf{x}+(\\mathbf{y}+\\mathbf{z})} & {\\color{black}\\text{[A6]}}:{\\color{blue}\\alpha (\\beta \\mathbf{x})=(\\alpha \\beta )\\mathbf{x}} \\\\ {\\color{black}\\text{[A3]}}:{\\color{blue}\\mathbf{x}+\\mathbf{0}=\\mathbf{x}} & {\\color{black}\\text{[A7]}}:{\\color{blue}(\\alpha +\\beta )\\mathbf{x}=\\alpha \\mathbf{x}+\\beta \\mathbf{x}} \\\\ {\\color{black}\\text{[A4]}}:{\\color{blue}\\mathbf{x}+(-\\mathbf{x})=\\mathbf{0}} & {\\color{black}\\text{[A8]}}:{\\color{blue}\\alpha (\\mathbf{x}+\\mathbf{y})=\\alpha \\mathbf{x}+\\alpha \\mathbf{y}}\\end{array}\n$$"] [17592186243985 "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n*If $\\mathbf{y}$ and $\\mathbf{z}$ are vectors such that $\\mathbf{x}+\\mathbf{y}=\\mathbf{z}+\\mathbf{x}$ for some $\\mathbf{x}\\in V$, then $\\mathbf{y}=\\mathbf{z}.$*\n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{x}+\\mathbf{y} & =\\mathbf{z}+\\mathbf{x} &  & [\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{given}\\hspace{0.222em}] \\\\ (\\mathbf{x}+\\mathbf{y})+(-\\mathbf{x}) & =(\\mathbf{z}+\\mathbf{x})+(-\\mathbf{x}) &  & [\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{add }-\\mathbf{x}\\text{ to both sides}\\hspace{0.222em}] \\\\ (\\mathbf{y}+